For a polynomial g(x) with real coefficients, let $m_{g}$ denote the number of distinct real roots of g(x). Suppose S is the set of polynomials with real coefficients defined by

$S = \{ {({x^2} - 1)^2}({a_0} + {a_1}x + {a_2}{x^2} + {a_3}{x^3}):{a_0},{a_1},{a_2},{a_3} \in R\}$;

For a polynomial f, let f' and f'' denote its first and second order derivatives, respectively. Then the minimum possible value of ($m_{f'} + m_{f''}$), where f $\in$ S, is ..............
